msgctxt "#32090"
msgid "Local Files"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32091"
msgid "Recreate local NFO file from Chronicle's data"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32092"
msgid "Kodi always prefers a movie, TV show, or episode's own local NFO file over asking this scraper, even during an automatic library scan -- so anything already tagged by another tool (e.g. tinyMediaManager) may never actually reach Chronicle at all. Enabling this lets Chronicle write that local NFO from its own data -- but only as part of an explicit rebuild pass (the \"Rebuild local NFOs from Chronicle\" action below, or \"Automatically rebuild NFOs after every library scan\"), never during an ordinary scan, so getting new files into Kodi's library is never slowed down by a local-file write. On by default -- this is what lets a rebuild pass actually close the loop and get new/changed episodes pushed to Kodi. Safe to leave on across every Kodi instance sharing the same library: Chronicle's own rebuild queue coordinates which single device actually does the delete-and-rewrite for any given item, so multiple instances no longer race each other rewriting the same shared NFO. Turn it off on a specific device only if you'd rather it never participate in rebuilds at all."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32093"
msgid "Rebuild local NFOs from Chronicle"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32094"
msgid "This will delete every local .nfo/tvshow.nfo file and every movieset-poster/fanart/etc. file for every movie, TV show, and episode in your library, then ask Chronicle to rebuild them one by one. Before deleting, any data a local NFO has that Chronicle doesn't is saved and folded back in (and sent to Chronicle), and any movieset-* art is copied into your Movie Set Information folder if nothing is there already -- so a previous tool's (e.g. tinyMediaManager) data is preserved, not lost. It can take a long time for a large library. Continue?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32095"
msgid "Delete and rebuild"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32096"
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32097"
msgid "All {0} items (movies, TV shows, and episodes) were rebuilt successfully."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32100"
msgid "Chronicle will rebuild your library's local NFOs in the background, one item at a time (delete, then rebuild, before moving to the next) -- you don't need to keep watching this, and can carry on using Kodi normally (including playback) while it finishes. There's no way to cancel once this starts; close Kodi if you need to stop it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32101"
msgid "Rebuilt {0} of {1} items -- {2} didn't complete. See kodi.log for details."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32102"
msgid "You stopped this before it finished -- Chronicle had gotten through {0} of {1} items. Whatever was already in progress keeps running in the background even now this is closed. Run it again later if you want to make sure everything gets covered."
msgstr ""

