msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32098"
msgid "Automatically rebuild NFOs after every library scan"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32099"
msgid "Runs the same delete-and-rebuild as \"Rebuild local NFOs from Chronicle\" above, automatically, every time a video library scan finishes -- no need to remember to click the button. Every local .nfo/tvshow.nfo and movieset-poster/fanart/etc. file for every movie, TV show, and episode is deleted and repopulated from Chronicle each time, with NO confirmation prompt (there's no one there to ask). Data only some other tool put in those files is preserved and folded back in rather than lost, but this still means a large library can take a long time to process on every single scan. On by default -- this is the only mechanism that reliably confirms a new or changed episode actually reached Kodi (Kodi never re-asks this scraper about an item once it has any local NFO at all); turn it off only if you'd rather trigger \"Rebuild local NFOs from Chronicle\" yourself, or if this is a secondary Kodi instance pointed at a library another instance already maintains."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32105"
msgid "Include technical file info (resolution, codec, HDR, audio, subtitles)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32106"
msgid "Adds a <fileinfo><streamdetails> block to the NFO with Kodi's own probe of the real file -- video codec/resolution/HDR type, audio codec/language/channels, subtitle track languages. This is data only Kodi itself has; Chronicle has no way to supply it. Requires an extra lookup against Kodi's own library on top of the normal NFO write, so it's off by default -- if you run this addon on more than one Kodi instance pointed at the same shared library, you only need this ON for whichever one is responsible for maintaining the shared NFOs; the others just read the NFO that instance already wrote, streamdetails included, so there's nothing to gain (and real extra work to lose) by also turning this on for them."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32107"
msgid "{0} item(s) processed so far{1}"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32108"
msgid "\"Rebuild local NFOs from Chronicle\" needs the \"Recreate local NFO file from Chronicle's data\" setting on first -- otherwise this would delete your existing local NFOs and never write new ones back, leaving your library with none at all. Turn it on and continue?"
msgstr ""

